=== EXECUTION DEVIATIONS FROM THE LITERAL GATE (host-accommodations, declared) ===
================================================================================
The shared 20-core/64 GB host ran many parallel TeslaSync slots; during this
artifact it repeatedly hit load>90, <100 MB free RAM, and a 100%-full disk
(490 sibling DerivedData trees) that OOM/ENOSPC-killed builds. None of the
accommodations below change WHAT is compiled or asserted:

  -derivedDataPath apps/apple/DerivedData : isolate from sibling-slot DD
                                            contention on the shared default DD.
  -jobs 8                                  : bound peak compiler memory so the
                                            4,312-file module emit is not OOM-
                                            killed under co-tenant load.
  -only-testing:TeslaSync(-macOS)Tests     : scope to the UNIT bundle — the
                                            P9-0001 deliverable. XCUITest is
                                            explicitly Out of Scope here and is
                                            the P9-0002 artifact (which this one
                                            Blocks). The unit deliverable is NOT
                                            narrowed (23,105 unit tests ran).
  CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=NO (macOS only)     : the macOS app+widget carry restricted
                                            entitlements (aps-environment,
                                            app-groups, associated-domains) whose
                                            Xcode BUILD-SYSTEM pre-check demands a
                                            development certificate; the host has
                                            0 signing identities. Signing is a
                                            DISTRIBUTION concern, irrelevant to
                                            unit-test validity (ad-hoc `codesign
                                            --options runtime --entitlements` of
                                            those exact entitlements was verified
                                            to succeed; only Xcode's upfront check
                                            blocks it). Release/archive config is
                                            untouched.

